  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sounds &amp; Stories of Stone Town: Connecting Culture and Community through Sustainable Tourism</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports local artists, youth, and women in Stone Town, Zanzibar to benefit more from tourism by connecting culture, heritage, and community-based experiences. It will strengthen skills in cultural tourism, creative business development, and storytelling while creating new opportunities for income and participation. Key activities include training programmes, cultural nights, youth creative markets, heritage tours, and support for festivals that promote local music, food, arts, and traditions. The project will also document traditional Taarab music, create partnerships with hotels and tour operators, and develop a shared heritage pass to encourage visitors to experience Zanzibar&#x2019;s living culture in a sustainable and inclusive way.</narrative>
  </description>
